  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "The three completed experiments (all scgpt+resnet50, multiprofile) show a clear trend: avgpool+weighted (0.525) > avgpool+concat (0.512) > transformer+concat (0.471). The aggregation/fusion choice is now well-characterized. The largest untested variable is the image encoder—ResNet50 is a relatively modest backbone, while ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L is substantially more expressive. Config_035 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the direct, minimal extension of our best result (config_011), swapping only the image encoder. This tests whether the image modality is a bottleneck and whether a stronger visual representation can push accuracy above 0.525. It is the highest-impact single change remaining in the design space. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~6–7 GPU hrs), roughly 1.5× the ResNet50-based configs due to ViT-L's larger parameter count, but well below the transformer-aggregation cost. With 6 experiments left, this is the best use of the next slot: it exploits the proven avgpool+weighted strategy while exploring the most consequential untested axis."
}

